# Build artifacts. Unanchored on purpose: this is a cargo workspace, and
# `/target/` matched only the root one — a member's `test-support/target/`
# slipped straight past it and got committed once already.
target/

# GoReleaser's output directory: the release archives, checksums, and the
# binaries they were built from. `task release:snapshot` fills it locally and
# `--clean` empties it first, so nothing here is ever worth keeping.
/dist/

# The release body the workflow extracts from CHANGELOG.md before publishing.
# Written by .github/scripts/extract-changelog.sh, which is also runnable
# locally to preview it.
/release-body.md

# Test scratch
/coverage/
*.profraw

# insta pending snapshots. Regenerated output, not stale leftovers: every run
# of a failing snapshot test rewrites its .snap.new, so these reappear after
# any red run and are never worth committing. (The rule was added when 20
# snapshot tests were failing at once; those were repaired in bds-04l.3 and
# the suite is green, but the rule still earns its place the next time one
# breaks.) Failing snapshots are reported by name by `task test:report`, which
# is more precise than `git status` and does not depend on this rule.
*.snap.new

# Beads runtime state is NOT listed here. `.beads/.gitignore` covers it, is
# written by `br init`, and takes precedence for everything under `.beads/`
# anyway — `git check-ignore -v` named that file, never this one, for every
# runtime path. Duplicating the rules here only created a second place to
# forget to update.

# Local databases
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Configuration
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
